---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import mark from "../assets/brand/kns-mark.png";
---
<Base title="About the Studio" description="Kuro Neko Sama Studios is a small indie studio making games and books: Heroes of Lumora, Aldenexia: Lightfall and Zen Divers.">
  <div class="wrap page-hero about">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1>A small studio with a big world.</h1>
      <p>Kuro Neko Sama Studios is Ross's indie game and book studio. We make the games, and Ross writes the books.</p>
    </div>
    <Image src={mark} alt="Kuro Neko Sama Studios cat mark" width={260} />
  </div>
  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Where it started</h2>
      <p>Aldenexia began when Ross was a child, in notebooks. Maps, lists of characters, towns and enemies, and his own player's guide and dungeon master's guide, the way a Dungeons &amp; Dragons world is built. He always wanted to bring that world to life, so other people could walk around in it too.</p>

      <h2>The games that shaped it</h2>
      <p><strong>Pool of Radiance</strong> felt enormous, and it was unforgiving: long fights against overwhelming numbers, and party members who could die along the way. The <strong>Ultima</strong> series, which Ross played start to finish, gave him companions who followed you from game to game and felt like real friends, people you actually cared about.</p>
      <p>Then came <strong>EverQuest</strong>, and the sheer size of it. Seeing the Nexus spires for the first time and having no idea what they were. Fighting minotaurs in the Gorge of King Xorbb, far from home, knowing a death meant a twenty- or thirty-minute run back. Fighting through Permafrost to reach Lady Vox for the first time, and the thrill of making it. That sense of wonder, and of a world big enough to be a little afraid of, is the bar we're reaching for.</p>

      <h2>Two games, one world</h2>
      <p>Heroes of Lumora and Aldenexia: Lightfall are both steps toward it. Heroes is the fast one: a fantasy bullet-hell set in the town of Lumora that you can finish in an evening and keep coming back to. Lightfall is the long one: a multiplayer RPG about exploring that world, with companions who carry the story alongside you, and living with your choices. They share a home, and some of the same people.</p>
      <p>Ross writes music too. At the Sunlit Rest, Lumora's tavern, the Songweaver Annadaeus sings one of his songs: "ZugZwang."</p>

      <h2>Where it's headed</h2>
      <p>The goal is a full world: a starting area for every race, group dungeons, and that feeling of stepping into somewhere new and huge with no idea what's over the next hill.</p>

      <h2>The books</h2>
      <p><a href="/books/"><em>Zen Divers</em></a> grew out of Ross's years of teaching scuba, and <em>The Lost Art of Being an Asshole</em> is about truth and Stoicism in modern life. Both are out on Amazon.</p>
      <p>We used to publish under two names, Kuro Neko Sama Games and KNS Books. As of late 2026 it's all one: Kuro Neko Sama Studios.</p>
      <div class="btns"><a class="btn primary" href="/world/">Explore the world</a><a class="btn ghost" href="/games/">See the games</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  .about { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; gap: 40px; align-items: center; text-align: left; }
  .about p { margin-left: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .about { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .about :global(img) { width: 160px; } }
</style>
